   "id": "c01",
   "text": "1789. Paris is *starving.*",
   "frames": 120
  },
  {
   "id": "c02",
   "text": "The queen says: let them eat *cake.*",
   "frames": 90
  },
  {
   "id": "c03",
   "text": "Except... she *never said it.*",
   "frames": 72
  },
  {
   "id": "c04",
   "text": "Marie Antoinette: *the cake myth.*",
   "frames": 66
  },
  {
   "id": "c05",
   "text": "The line comes from a book by *Rousseau.*",
   "frames": 98
  },
  {
   "id": "c06",
   "text": "He wrote that around *1765.*",
   "frames": 115
  },
  {
   "id": "c07",
   "text": "About \"a great princess.\" *No name.*",
   "frames": 104
  },
  {
   "id": "c08",
   "text": "In 1765, Marie Antoinette was *nine.*",
   "frames": 137
  },
  {
   "id": "c09",
   "text": "And living in *Austria.*",
   "frames": 74
  },
  {
   "id": "c10",
   "text": "Also, he wrote *brioche.* Not cake.",
   "frames": 103
  },
  {
   "id": "c11",
   "text": "Wrong age. Wrong country. *Wrong pastry.*",
   "frames": 114
  },
  {
   "id": "c12",
   "text": "During a bread riot, she wrote they must help the *people.*",
   "frames": 130
  },
  {
   "id": "c13",
   "text": "But the revolution needed a *villain.*",
   "frames": 94
  },
  {
   "id": "c14",
   "text": "Nasty pamphlets made her the *bad guy.*",
   "frames": 107
  },
  {
   "id": "c15",
   "text": "The quote got pinned on her, and it *stuck.*",
   "frames": 101
  },
  {
   "id": "c16",
   "text": "Today it's on mugs and *t-shirts.*",
   "frames": 100
  },
  {
   "id": "c17",
   "text": "Who really said it? *Nobody knows.*",
   "frames": 94
  },
  {
   "id": "c18",
   "text": "Cakes offered by Marie Antoinette: *zero.*",
   "frames": 113
  },
  {
   "id": "c19",
